          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:628c6e14944482da4fac6d42d50730e54386313980f57d27dd54466c9d55200d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_63286768e9074ab09f76c1c29bd2fea6",
      "statement": "RenewWithToken builds a JWT with audience <ca-url>/renew, issuer step-ca-client/1.0, subject from the leaf common name, and the certificate chain in the x5cInsecure header, signed with the certificate key; it clears the transport's client certificate and closes idle connections before client.RenewWithToken.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L621-L653",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b4ad0112ba3a924907f740ef6ed256613c2dbe75427795bb384fd104a748a422:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_69c78ed3f69a4ea38c60e306f3702d23",
      "statement": "The renewed certificate chain is serialized as PEM and written with fileutil.WriteFile mode 0600, to --out or overwriting the input certificate file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L482-L507",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:23d4086ec109b09dad7f4fad44ac8d800cf731e01508d452d94691a2aae385f2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c42d9ed5b8034b26ae8016ebe6d45ffa",
      "statement": "--renew-period requires --daemon, is mutually exclusive with --expires-in, and both must be shorter than the certificate validity period or the command errors.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L262-L278",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9ec52b529c140fac16de7a5ec051b944d908978eafcc9ac467478a6e809d74c5:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L313-L321",
