        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a0fe7942feca4c48b93bfd14fe45ac6e",
      "statement": "nextRenewDuration implements the timing model: with --renew-period the delay is the period (renewing immediately if the remaining lifetime is below it); otherwise the window defaults to one third of the validity (renew before 2/3 elapsed) with random jitter bounded by period/20, renewing immediately when already inside the window.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L354-L380",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:01ffbad2ae3f1aae3edb8f558cef5e6ddc34ca88f58078614ce4581c2896bcf8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a2182da98d6747c7ba56379f04111f51",
      "statement": "Daemon mode forces overwrite, handles SIGHUP as immediate renewal and SIGINT/SIGTERM as clean exit, reloads the new chain into the TLS transport after each renewal, and waits a fixed 1 minute after errors before retrying.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L586-L619",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7395063303b8948af0df0e6f18704405d3eecdc99e3e6a5ca9c278e07af0d001:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ca03be98bb8e4feca121b6be0ad19791",
      "statement": "After renewal (or a one-shot renewal), --pid or --pid-file (mutually exclusive, positive) signals a process with --signal (default SIGHUP), and --exec runs the given command split on spaces with inherited stdio.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://command/ca/renew.go#L280-L306",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:099ab502e7ad66998da4b743d440fef7cc4d850a2ba0f254ebd56d6f78aa1a56:"
